# rendered videos — regenerate with `ci-video render`
out/

# generated compositions — regenerate with `ci-video build`
build/

# playwright auth state
.auth/

node_modules/

# captured screenshots ARE COMMITTED — see assets/shots/.
#
# They used to be ignored here, on the reasoning that capturing locally is cheap
# and a stale committed screenshot outlives the UI it photographed. That trade
# only holds if everyone can re-capture, and fleet-wide they cannot: as of
# 2026-08-05 only three of twelve products have a stage that actually comes up.
# A gitignored shot set therefore means nobody but the stage's author can render
# the cut, and eleven of twelve products were rendering every screen beat as a
# "capture pending" slate.
#
# So the shots are inputs, checked in like any other input. Staleness is the
# cost we accept for a render anyone can reproduce; re-run `./video/make.sh`
# when the UI moves and commit the new PNGs in the same change.

# npm install writes this when the toolchain is installed; the project has never
# had one and both make.sh and the workflow use `npm install`, so committing it
# now would quietly change how the video toolchain resolves.
package-lock.json
